v3.8.18
the agent places no order on a DO request created more than
  do_request_max_age_seconds before the timestamp of the chain's latest
  block, on every network and whether the request is pinned to the node or
  not: DO_REQUEST_MAX_AGE_SECONDS in node/.env (86400 s), replaced for one
  network by <NETWORK>_DO_REQUEST_MAX_AGE_SECONDS in the environment or by
  the argument --<network>_do_request_max_age_seconds, which stands before
  it (config.NetworkConfig.do_request_max_age_seconds, at least 1 s). The
  rule holds where the agent places, the intake loop (process_dp_request,
  place_order); a reserved order the broker places on the node's offer and
  an order the node placed that is approved after its window are run
  whatever their DO request's age
a DO request's createdAt, uint32 of the timestamp of the block that added
  it, is read with eth_getStorageAt (do_request_age.py). Where the PoX
  answers ethStorageAddress(), from the storage it names, layout cloud
  (EthernityCloudStorage: doRequestsList's length at slot 3, 10 slots a
  request, createdAt the low 32 bits of slot keccak256(3) + 10 id + 1);
  where it does not, from the PoX itself, layout v05 (doRequestsList's
  length at slot 19, 9 slots a request, createdAt the top 32 bits of slot
  keccak256(19) + 9 id). bloxberg_mainnet (PoX
  0x549A6E06BB2084100148D50F51CF77a3436C3Ae7) is read as v05; the storages
  of the other networks, read as cloud: bloxberg_testnet and
  bloxberg_testnet_unsafe 0xEE3aAa1A7a8C00BeBBb5DfC570F80f6FA12a968d,
  polygon_mainnet 0x6aAafE99746Bd9f9258DbC1A8C82f3C15563636C, polygon_amoy
  and polygon_amoy_unsafe 0xD7f6826EeC7606E41198CD06C2147645bD15AC9d,
  iotex_testnet 0xD6AF20E8E03e18e42E42DFAa6EC0c559301A5523, ethereum_sepolia
  and ethereum_sepolia_unsafe 0x02882F03097fE8cD31afbdFbB5D72a498B41112c,
  litvm_liteforge and litvm_liteforge_unsafe
  0x41269644d3a4Cd29ec01fbB6abcDCE93A99fDF0b. A layout is taken when its
  length slot lies within 16 of the DO request count read before it and the
  newest request both hold has a createdAt from 2020-01-01 to 60 s after the
  latest block's timestamp; the line "DO request ages: createdAt is read
  from <address> (layout <name>)" names it
a pass with a DO request to judge reads the latest block and establishes the
  age boundary, the lowest id created at or after its timestamp less the
  limit: requests are appended in block order, so createdAt does not
  decrease with the id; the search reads the boundary of the pass before,
  then binary-searches the ids above it, and the boundary never moves back.
  The pass judges the ids from the boundary on and never reads a request
  below it. "DO requests below <boundary> (of <count>) were created more
  than <limit> s before block <number> (<time>); none of them is judged or
  placed" is logged when the boundary moves. A pass whose every request from
  the boundary on is in doreq_cache.txt or held for its resources reads
  neither the latest block nor the storage
a pass whose boundary is not established places no order, and the next pass
  tries again: a layout or a createdAt that is not plausible is logged at
  ERROR ("DO request ages are not established (<reason>); no order is placed
  until they are"), an RPC failure or a createdAt of 0, a request the RPC's
  node does not hold yet, at WARNING ("DO request ages were not read
  (<error>); no order is placed this pass"), each at most once an hour per
  network. After a createdAt that is not plausible or is 0 the storage and
  layout are established again
the boundary's reads, each after the network's RPC delay: the latest block
  (eth_getBlockByNumber, one request); on a handle's first boundary
  ethStorageAddress() (three requests: eth_chainId, eth_call, eth_chainId),
  the length slot and the newest request (eth_getStorageAt, one request
  each); then the boundary before, and at most ceil(log2(count - boundary))
  more when it moved. A handle's first boundary posts 6 + 1 +
  ceil(log2(count)) requests at most, 23 on 34,542 DO requests; a boundary
  that has not moved posts 2. At polygon_mainnet's 200 ms the boundary
  sleeps 0.4 s before a placement on a bound handle, 1.0 s on a handle's
  first boundary

v3.8.17
the registered-image pin reads the IPFS repository's size before it starts
  (utils.Storage.repo_size, Kubo's repo/stat) up to three times, 5 s apart,
  and the attempt fails at the third failure; the pin's watch reads the size
  every 10 s, one read each, and ends the pin at three failed reads in a row
Kubo answers repo/stat with 500 ("getting disk usage at /: lstat
  /data/ipfs/datastore/<n>.ldb: no such file or directory") when leveldb
  removes a file while the read walks the datastore

v3.8.16
Polygon mainnet's default delay between the agent's chain calls is 200 ms
  (POLYGON_MAINNET_RPC_DELAY in node/.env), the delay of every network but
  the bloxberg testnet pair (0). Polygon mainnet's default RPC
  (https://polygon-bor-rpc.publicnode.com/) serves an address 1,200 requests
  in 60 s
a replication round (run_esr_replication_loop, every
  ESR_REPLICATION_INTERVAL_SECONDS) reads the newest 200 orders
  (ESR_RESULT_SCAN_ORDERS) and the newest 200 DO requests and orders
  (DO_REQUEST_SCAN_REQUESTS), sleeping the delay before each; at 200 ms a
  round sleeps at least 160 s once the PoX holds 200 orders. A new DO request
  is seen up to 0.19 s later and its placement sent 0.38 to 0.57 s later; a
  node without doreq_cache.txt takes up to 0.19 s more for each DO request of
  its first pass
the delay of one node, 0 or more whole milliseconds, is set by
  POLYGON_MAINNET_RPC_DELAY in the service's environment (a drop-in of
  etny-node.service) or by the argument --polygon_mainnet_rpc_delay, which
  stands before it; config.parse_networks reads the process's environment,
  into which load_dotenv puts node/.env's values only for the variables that
  are not set. A start script with parse_config_to_args
  (ubuntu/etny-node-start.sh) passes the config line
  POLYGON_MAINNET_RPC_DELAY=<milliseconds> of /home/vagrant/etny/node/config
  as that argument; a start script without it passes no config line. The
  start script resets the checkout, node/.env included, to origin/master at
  every start

v3.8.15
Polygon mainnet's default fee ceiling is 500 gwei
  (POLYGON_MAINNET_MAX_FEE_PER_GAS in node/.env). On Polygon mainnet the agent
  builds its offer, heartbeat, placement and result with maxFeePerGas
  int(baseFee * 1.1) plus the priority fee of 32 gwei (get_transaction_build),
  paid in POL from its own wallet, and sends none above the ceiling ("Network
  base fee is too high!"); 500 gwei admits a base fee up to 425.4 gwei
the ceiling of one node, in gwei, is set by POLYGON_MAINNET_MAX_FEE_PER_GAS in
  the service's environment (a drop-in of etny-node.service) or by the
  argument --polygon_mainnet_max_fee_per_gas, which stands before it;
  config.parse_networks reads the process's environment, into which
  load_dotenv puts node/.env's values only for the variables that are not set.
  A start script with parse_config_to_args (ubuntu/etny-node-start.sh) passes
  the config line POLYGON_MAINNET_MAX_FEE_PER_GAS=<gwei> of
  /home/vagrant/etny/node/config as that argument. The start script resets the
  checkout, node/.env included, to origin/master at every start

v3.8.14
the enclave composes get ETNY_SCONE_QUEUES per network: every docker-compose
  run on an order's or an integration test's compose (pull, down, up) takes
  the agent's environment with the count of the network's PoX generation
  (utils.enclave_compose_env), twice the node's CPUs within 4 and 64 on a
  PoX 1.2 and within 4 and 8 (utils.SCONE_QUEUES_LEGACY_MAX) on a legacy PoX,
  whose trustedzone images are signed without --tcs and take at most eight
  queues; the agent's own environment is not given the variable (one process
  serves networks of both generations), and the start line "SCONE queues for
  the enclaves" follows the network's pox= line and names the count and the
  generation

v3.8.13
the capability record's compute figure is gflops, whole GFLOPS of the
  benchmark kernel under cuv 4 (one CU is 100 GFLOPS, utils.GFLOPS_PER_CU):
  the agent admits its own record at cuv CU_VERSION_MIN (4) and above with
  gflops at most CU_MAX_GFLOPS (6400, CU_MAX 64 x 100), the gflops bound
  checked first as the validators check it; a stored record (in
  node/<network>/capability.json) below CU_VERSION_MIN or without gflops is
  dropped when the store loads, the test's pass kept with retest_pending set
  in the file until the next pass (RecordStore.retest_pending), and its
  integration test runs again, after a restart as well; an admitted record is
  logged as "record admitted (gflops N (x.xx CU), cuv M, ..."
addDPRequestV2 carries the record's gflops (0 without a record, recorded by
  the contract at 100), metadata4 carries cugflops=<gflops>, and the tip per
  CU-hour spreads the node's own gas over gflops / 100 CU
  (utils.tip_per_cu_hour_wei); the pre-filter refuses a V2 DO request whose
  maxGflops is below the node's gflops (Refusal kind gflops, cached), and the
  placement refusal "node above maxGflops" names the offer
the validators' cancel reasons 6 GflopsAboveMax and 8 CuVersionBelowMinimum
  (capability.CANCEL_REASONS) re-test the record before the re-add
  (RETEST_REASONS 1..6, 8 and 9); 7 DeliveredBelowAttested re-adds
the validators' cancel reason 9 RecordMissing (an offer without a capability
  record that the validators do not pass over: its trustedzones= list names
  none, names a trustedzone without the -unsafe suffix, or the network admits
  no -unsafe trustedzone)
  sets the network's RecordMissing hold (capability.RecordMissingHold, kept
  under record_missing_hold in node/<network>/broker_cursor.json, written
  before the scan's cursor moves, so a restart keeps it): the agent posts no
  DP request without a record on that network unless the request names only
  -unsafe trustedzones (capability.unsafe_only, the offer the validators pass
  over) (add_dp_request, the request sent with a result and the idle tick's
  replacement), logs the hold once per change and waits
  RECORD_MISSING_POLL_SECONDS (60) between its looks for a record, running
  meanwhile the idle duties that need no standing request (the heartbeat,
  the IPFS cleanup and peering, an order approved after its window, the
  broker's tick); the passed tests whose image requires dcap and whose pass
  holds no record run again at once, and while they pass without one they
  run again on the failure backoff (10 min doubling to 6 h); an advertised
  record clears the hold and the request carries it. A network whose
  validators never cancelled with reason 9 has no hold, and its agent posts
  a request without a record (where the validators do not vote, as on LitVM,
  it stands)
the DPRequestCancelled scan reads the cancels of every DP request of the
  node (the indexed dproc topic) from the persisted dp_request_cancelled
  cursor, before every add (a process start's first included, so a cancel
  that landed while the agent was stopped is seen) and at every idle tick;
  the reaction follows the record the cancelled request carried
  (capability.cancel_reaction over its cusig, RecordStore.image_of): a
  record reason on a request that carried a record drops that record and
  re-tests, a request without a record has none to drop
the bundled ABI files node/docker/pox.abi, node/reader.abi, node/pricing.abi
  and node/broker.abi are the pox-smart-contract-litvm exports with the GFLOPS
  names (gflops, maxGflops, minGflops, gflopsMax, gflopsMaxDefault,
  capacityGflops, loadGflops, reservedGflops, reservedCapacityGflops); the
  agent reads them as DORequestV2.max_gflops, DPTerms.gflops and
  OrderTerms.gflops, and accepted.json holds predecessor_gflops
  (broker.bounded_gflops)
bloxberg_testnet and bloxberg_testnet_unsafe bind the PoX 1.2 implementation
  0x830c781F0352050343211B6BFA83600B3e77647C, polygon_amoy and
  polygon_amoy_unsafe the PoX 1.2 implementation
  0xd1182deA61CDa785C320cdBE5888EaC4178cAAF2 (node/.env): the
  implementations of pox-smart-contract-litvm deployed 2026-11-18, whose
  compute figures are whole GFLOPS

